  "purpose": "Blind set for the Shopify engine: measurement only. Nobody opens, traces or debugs these repositories; it is run once, in the combined Shopify benchmark at the end.",
  "criteria": "GitHub code search (6 queries, each split into 5 file-size ranges; listed in search.queries), excluding every owner/name any file under docs/benchmarks names at HEAD and origin/main. Kept: not archived, not a fork, under 512 MB on GitHub; a default-branch commit since 2026-07-31 with at least 2 distinct human commit authors in that window (bots excluded); a .github/workflows directory; a root package.json and at least one root lockfile (package-lock.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, yarn.lock, bun.lock, bun.lockb). With fewer than 100 affected repositories, shopify-blind-100 loosens in order (founder, 2026-10-29): the activity window to 180 days, then 1 human author; each loosened stage is pre-scanned in seeded order only until the set is full, and each repository records the filters loosened for it (loosened). CI, lockfile, Shopify usage and affected checks never loosen. Pre-scan, offline, at the recorded commit: Refit's Shopify scan (pipeline/shopify-analysis.ts) and runPipeline from the pinned version's supported schema (the oldest supported, 2026-01, for older pins) to 2026-10. Affected when the oldest runtime pin (codegen configs excluded; LATEST_API_VERSION resolved through the locked SDK) is unsupported (before 2026-01) or retiring soonest (2026-01), the code calls the REST Admin API, a GraphQL document fails on 2026-10 or already fails (removed fields), or such a failing document is a product or variant mutation (product model). Split: affected repositories in the order of SHA-256(\"refit-shopify-2026-10-29\\n\" + lower-cased name). shopify-blind-100 takes up to 100 of the search's 100 affected repositories; shopify-dev-60 takes up to 60 affected repositories with a root lockfile from the already-open lists docs/benchmarks/2026-10-16-shopify-repos.json, docs/benchmarks/2026-10-16-shopify-fresh-repos.json, pre-scanned the same way at their frozen commits without the activity filters (145 of 250 affected). Command: GITHUB_TOKEN=… npx tsx scripts/shopify-select.mjs --work <dir> --frozen-at 2026-10-29 --seed refit-shopify-2026-10-29 --dev-from docs/benchmarks/2026-10-16-shopify-repos.json --dev-from docs/benchmarks/2026-10-16-shopify-fresh-repos.json",
